# Normalize text files to LF in the repository and in every working tree,
# including on Windows. Test inputs (conformance cases, the CommonMark suite)
# and expected outputs are compared byte for byte, so a checkout must not
# rewrite their line endings. A case that needs CRLF input marks its file
# with `-text` here.
* text=auto eol=lf

# A source file that must stay invalid UTF-8, byte for byte.
tests/conformance/cases/files/source-not-utf8/files/bad.md binary

# An example checked out with CRLF line endings, which its observation hashes
# as LF.
tests/conformance/cases/directives/snippet/tested-line/code/examples/crlf.ts -text
tests/conformance/cases/directives/snippet/tested-status/code/examples/crlf.ts -text

# A case whose frontmatter has a lone carriage return.
tests/conformance/cases/format/frontmatter-lone-carriage-return/input.md -text
tests/conformance/cases/format/frontmatter-lone-carriage-return/formatted.md -text
